  "problem": {
    "id": "train-2486",
    "question": "There are 248 pages in a book. Joanna can read 16 pages per hour. On Monday, she reads for 3 hours. On Tuesday, she reads for 6.5 hours. How many more hours does she need to read to finish the book?",
    "gold": "6",
    "answer": "On Monday, Joanna reads 3*16=<<3*16=48>>48 pages.\nOn Tuesday, Joanna reads 6.5 * 16 =<<6.5*16=104>>104 pages.\nSo far, she has read 48 +104 =<<48+104=152>>152 pages.\nThus, she has 248-152 = <<248-152=96>>96 pages left.\nShe will need to read for 96/16 = <<96/16=6>>6 hours to finish the book.\n#### 6"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many more hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pages Joanna reads on Monday.\n2. Calculate the total number of pages Joanna reads on Tuesday.\n3. Determine the total number of pages Joanna has read so far.\n4. Subtract the number of pages read so far from the total number of pages in the book to find out how many more pages she needs to read.\n5. Calculate the number of additional hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pages Joanna reads on Monday:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Pages read on Monday} = 16 \\text{ pages/hour} \\times 3 \\text{ hours} = 48 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the total number of pages Joanna reads on Tuesday:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Pages read on Tuesday} = 16 \\text{ pages/hour} \\times 6.5 \\text{ hours} = 104 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n3. Determine the total number of pages Joanna has read so far:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total pages read} = 48 \\text{ pages} + 104 \\text{ pages} = 152 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n4. Subtract the number of pages read so far from the total number of pages in the book to find out how many more pages she needs to read:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Pages left to read} = 248 \\text{ pages} - 152 \\text{ pages} = 96 \\text{ pages}\n   \\]\n\n5. Calculate the number of additional hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Additional hours needed} = \\frac{96 \\text{ pages}}{16 \\text{ pages/hour}} = 6 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of additional hours Joanna needs to read to finish the book is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
